.TH SFTP-COMMANDER 1 "2026-11-26" "sftp-commander 0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sftp-commander \- two-pane SFTP client in the style of WinSCP Commander
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sftp-commander
.RI [ server ]
.RB [ \-i
.IR keyfile ]
.br
.B sftp-commander \-\-prueba
.IR user @ host [: port ]
.RB [ \-i
.IR keyfile ]
.RB [ \-\-known\-hosts
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-aceptar\-host ]
.br
.B sftp-commander \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sftp-commander
is a graphical SFTP client for GTK 4. It shows the local computer and the
server side by side and copies files between them with the keyboard or the
right-click menu. Each tab holds an independent session. The user interface
is in Spanish.
.PP
It uses the standard OpenSSH files: aliases from
.IR ~/.ssh/config ,
host keys from
.IR ~/.ssh/known_hosts ,
keys from
.I ~/.ssh
and ssh-agent. Passwords are only stored, when the user asks for it, in the
system keyring through the Secret Service API.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I server
Connect on start. It can be the name of a saved server, an alias from
.IR ~/.ssh/config ,
.IR user @ host [: port ]
or an
.BI sftp:// user @ host [: port ]
URL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " keyfile"
Private key to use when connecting.
.TP
.BI \-J " user@host[:port]"
Connect through this jump server (bastion), like
.BR "ssh \-J" .
The destination is reached through an SSH tunnel opened on the jump server.
.TP
.BI \-\-known\-hosts " file"
Use this file instead of
.IR ~/.ssh/known_hosts .
.TP
.B \-\-prueba
Run an end-to-end SFTP test without a window against the given server and
exit with status 0 if everything worked. It creates and removes a temporary
folder in the remote home directory.
.TP
.B \-\-aceptar\-host
With
.BR \-\-prueba ,
accept and store an unknown host key.
.TP
.BI \-\-que\-app " file"
Print which application would be used to open
.I file
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TS
l l.
F4	Copy the selection to the other pane (asks first)
F5, Ctrl+R	Refresh both panes
Enter	Open or edit
F1	About
F2	Rename
F7	New folder
Shift+F4	New empty document
F8, Delete	Delete
Ctrl+F	Search in the current folder
Letters	Jump to the first name starting with them
Ctrl+Shift+C	Copy path
Ctrl+T, Ctrl+W	New tab, close tab
Ctrl+H	Show or hide hidden files
Ctrl+L	Manage saved servers
.TE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sftp-commander/servidores.ini
Saved servers (never contains passwords).
.TP
.I ~/.config/sftp-commander/preferencias.ini
Preferences, such as whether to ask before copying.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/sftp-commander/editar/
Temporary copies of remote files being edited; removed on exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sftp (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
.PP
The user guide is installed in
.IR /usr/share/doc/sftp-commander/ .
